 34P  dL E$Least-squares fitting is done by GLSC (version 12-Jun-2026)          
 34P  c  2006Kr07: a 140-MeV {+34}S beam was produced from the 15-UD Pelletron  
 34P 2c  accelerator at the Nuclear Science Centre, New Delhi, India. The target
 34P 3c  was 1.29-mg/cm{+2} enriched {+115}In. The deexciting |g rays were      
 34P 4c  detected using the Indian National Gamma Array (INGA), consisting of   
 34P 5c  eight Compton-suppressed HPGe Clover detectors. Measured E|g, I|g,     
 34P 6c  |g|g-coin, |g|g(|q)(DCO), and |g|g(|q)(POL). Deduced levels, J, |p, and
 34P 7c  |g-ray multipolarities. Comparisons with shell-model calculations.     
 34P  cG E,RI$From 2006Kr07. |DE|g=1 keV is assumed by evaluators based on      
 34P 2cG typical uncertainties for the INGA array.                              
 34P  cG M$From measured |g|g(|q)(DCO) and |g|g(|q)(POL). Expected R{-DCO}      
 34P 2cG values in a stretched quadrupole gate are R{-DCO}(Q)|?1.05 for         
 34P 3cG stretched quadrupole (|DJ=2) or unstretched dipole (|DJ=0) transitions;
 34P 4cG R{-DCO}(Q)|?0.55 for stretched dipole (|DJ=1) transitions. Expected    
 34P 5cG R{-DCO} values in a stretched dipole gate are R{-DCO}(D)|?1.1 for      
 34P 6cG stretched dipole (|DJ=1) transitions; R{-DCO}(D)|?1.8 for stretched    
 34P 7cG quadrupole (|DJ=2) or unstretched dipole (|DJ=0) transitions. A        
 34P 8cG positive POL indicates an electric type transition, and a negative POL 
 34P 9cG indicates a magnetic type transition.                                  
 34P  cL E$From a least-squares fit to the measured |g-ray energies, unless     
 34P 2cL otherwise noted.                                                       
 34P  cL J$As given in 2006Kr07. When considered in the Adopted Levels, the firm
 34P 2cL assignments here are placed within parentheses if there are no other   
 34P 3cL strong arguments to support these firm assignments.                    
